        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Timothy Day",
          "email": "timday@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-10-20 18:13:48.000000000",
          "tz": -240
        },
        "subject": "LU-20999 utils: remove lctl getattr and setattr commands",
        "message": "LU-20999 utils: remove lctl getattr and setattr commands\n\nlctl getattr and setattr issued OBD_IOC_GETATTR and OBD_IOC_SETATTR\nagainst the echo client, and test_getattr and test_setattr looped\nthe same ioctls as micro-benchmarks. Nothing in the test suite or\nlustre-iokit uses setattr or either test_ command. The only getattr\ncaller was the obdecho_test helper in sanity.sh test 180, which\nadded it in LU-3267 as a regression check for the echo sequence\nhandling in the ioctl. The echo client no longer takes a bare object\nid without a sequence, and test_brw already exercises the same\nobject lookup path, so the check is redundant.\n\nRemove all four commands and their jt_obd_getattr(),\njt_obd_setattr(), jt_obd_test_getattr() and jt_obd_test_setattr()\nhandlers, the private jt_str_to_ost_id() helper, the OBD_IOC_GETATTR\nand OBD_IOC_SETATTR handlers in the echo client and OSC, and the\ngetattr step from obdecho_test(). Keep the ioctl numbers reserved in\nthe UAPI header.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nSigned-off-by: Timothy Day <timday@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: I0d48f2c88bdf3e59cd12b004b04c5bcb6a6a6964\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
